($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 13869480, $f$
      Ready and Waiting$f$, ARRAY[$f$Vacillating$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$Sins of the Cities Series - K. J. Charles$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$Nathaniel hadn’t known what to expect when he invited Justin, and Sukey and Emma, to come to Harpenden for Christmas. He certainly hadn’t been expecting this... but he is going to enjoy it. In short: Justin likes to experiment - on Nathaniel.$f$, 971, 1, 1, true, 5, false, $f$2019-02-26T12:23:43.120+00:00$f$, $f$2019-02-26T12:23:43.161+00:00$f$, $f$2018-03-04T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 13878786, $f$When Shadows Fill Our Day$f$, ARRAY[$f$roseandheather$f$]::text[], ARRAY[$f$Call the Midwife$f$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], $f$Val doesn't believe in God. Maybe she did, once, before any trace of faith was seared away by war and loss and grief. Maybe she did before she watched good men die, men she couldn't save, men who begged for their mothers and sobbed with agony, men who died weeping or lived forever maimed.She doesn't believe in God, but she knows Lucille does, and hopes that it helps her. Hopes that it gives her some comfort, some grace.She thinks Barbara would approve of that, if anyone would.$f$, 811, 1, 1, true, 3, false, $f$2019-06-01T20:23:28.885+00:00$f$, $f$2019-06-01T20:23:28.889+00:00$f$, $f$2018-03-05T00:00:00.000+00:00$f$, false, false, true, NULL, NULL, ARRAY[]::text[]),
($f$080b7013-14b2-4fd8-be8b-f567db3cdb39$f$, 13879074, $f$
